From: Lilya <lilya@localhost>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gtkapplication-wayland: Skip session removal on window forget

File Roller can destroy its batch-operation dialog after the Wayland surface
has entered teardown. GTK 4.22.4 then reaches
gdk_wayland_toplevel_remove_from_session() with a stale toplevel and crashes.

Skip this optional session bookkeeping for the app-local GTK build used only by
File Roller. Window destruction and the parent GtkApplication bookkeeping still
run normally, and the application remains on native Wayland.

Remove once GTK's Wayland session removal is safe during late window teardown.
---
 gtk/gtkapplication-wayland.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gtk/gtkapplication-wayland.c b/gtk/gtkapplication-wayland.c
index 2158cf666e6..9d3f4cf1f76 100644
--- a/gtk/gtkapplication-wayland.c
+++ b/gtk/gtkapplication-wayland.c
@@ -230,2 +229,0 @@ gtk_application_impl_wayland_window_forget (GtkApplicationImpl *impl,
-  GdkSurface *surface;
-
@@ -234,2 +232 @@ gtk_application_impl_wayland_window_forget (GtkApplicationImpl *impl,
-  surface = gtk_native_get_surface (GTK_NATIVE (window));
-  gdk_wayland_toplevel_remove_from_session (GDK_TOPLEVEL (surface));
+  /* File Roller uses an app-local GTK build which omits late session cleanup. */
